    "notes": "This work draws from the visual tradition of American tonalism and early pictorial photography, where restraint and atmosphere carry more weight than detail alone. The softened edges and aged palette echo the influence of 19th-century painters and illustrators who treated buildings as living participants in the landscape rather than static subjects.\n\nWeathered Home rewards slow viewing. Its strength lies not in nostalgia, but in quiet permanence—an image that settles into a space and continues to speak long after first encounter.",
